{"availability":"available","full":"jo-duchan/tapflow","name":"tapflow","description":"Self-hosted iOS & Android simulator streaming for the whole team","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":839,"forks":96,"created":"2026-05-07T15:34:29Z","updated":"2026-10-08T15:57:36Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://www.tapflow.dev","topics":["android","android-emulator","app-testing","appetize-alternative","browserstack-alternative","developer-tools","emulator","flutter","good-first-issue","ios","ios-simulator","mcp","mobile-qa","mobile-testing","open-source","qa-tools","react-native","self-hosted","simulator","testing"],"demo":"https://www.tapflow.dev/get-started/introduction","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:16.303Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:16.303Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:05:16.303Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-04T08:16:58.062Z","stars":816,"forks":95},{"at":"2026-10-06T15:45:33.787Z","stars":836,"forks":96},{"at":"2026-10-08T16:05:16.303Z","stars":839,"forks":96}],"technologies":["React","Flutter"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Streams over H.264 with a zero-buffer decoder (no MSE) — latency measurements ↗","v0.x, actively developed — backward-compatible by default; breaking changes are rare and always noted in the changelog. Roadmap →","Mobile QA usually depends on access to simulators, emulators, or physical devices — and that access is uneven across a team."],"features":["No mobile toolchain for QA users — teammates test from a browser without installing Xcode, Android Studio, or local simulator tooling.","Self-hosted by default — no third-party cloud and no external accounts; everything runs on hardware you already own.","Use your existing Mac setup — run agents on Macs that already have the iOS Simulator or Android emulator available.","Browser streaming — iOS & Android at 30 fps, no extra app on the device. Both stream H.264 through a 2-tier decoder (